ore protection than they delivered.\n\nTo be fair to the safetyist position: a weak lever beats no lever, and a first draft can pressure the legislature into passing something real. That's true, and it's the best defense of this order. But a draft only becomes law if somebody demands it. So here's the test for everyone in this debate. If your kill switch is real, name the threshold, name who can pull it, and name the penalty for ignoring it. If it's a press release with a switch drawn on it, say so — and then tell me who you think you're protecting. Right now, the people actually harmed by deployed AI — gig workers, denied claims, misidentified suspects — are being handed a symbol while the deployment continues. Who pays for that gap, and for how long?",
